# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# The clickable demo in QEMU. The input PD plays the
# host demo's session one step per frame; the display stub hashes each frame.
# Frame N's hash is that of the approved golden image of step N,
# crates/nowayos-demo/session/NN-*.png, as x8r8g8b8: the Pi 5's 1920x1080
# window at scale 2, drawn at its own pixels - a host test
# (crates/nowayos-demo/tests/frame_hash.rs) checks these lines against them.
# Frames 1 and 2 equal frame 0 (a tap outside every control and keys with
# nothing focused change nothing), and frame 9 equals it again (Start again).
NOWAYOS: display-stub: starting
NOWAYOS: display-stub: announced 1920x1080 Xrgb8888 at scale 2
NOWAYOS: input-script: starting; 10 steps to play
NOWAYOS: ui: starting
NOWAYOS: ui: the display is 1920x1080 Xrgb8888 at scale 2
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 0 hash 0x1eb8cb3c502ea8ef
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 1 hash 0x1eb8cb3c502ea8ef
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 2 hash 0x1eb8cb3c502ea8ef
NOWAYOS: ui: input record rejected: invalid value in field `tag`
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 3 hash 0xf7e7396b806d5adf
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 4 hash 0xa9dbda556c368e3a
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 5 hash 0x7012bfe5e1b88f4d
NOWAYOS: ui: action Help
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 6 hash 0xd56f21aa8cf2259d
NOWAYOS: ui: action Continue
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 7 hash 0x7197de60d8b874a4
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 8 hash 0x7197de60d8b874a4
NOWAYOS: ui: action Start again
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 9 hash 0x1eb8cb3c502ea8ef
NOWAYOS: ui: frame 9 shown
NOWAYOS: input-script: session done

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match).
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!refused
!cannot show frames
